Z||000000||Joe Torma||08-08-2001||04:58 PM||||I have seen some awesome cars here...and I want to put them ALL in a book.  <P>Stock, Modified, Rebodied, Works in progress...<BR>It will showcase your car(s) in a magazine style , but will be in a binder format so that updates can easily be inserted.  So don't feel bad if your car isn't quite done!  Also, this way you don't have a pile of magazines, just a nice protective binder of awesome Fieros.  You could add your own personal photopages too.<P>Brainstorming on another thread, a couple of us came up with a few ideas.<P>*Book divided into body styles GTs, SEs, etc..<BR>*Fiero history (someone wanted to do this before this)<BR>*Story on how you found your car<BR>*Personal write-up<BR>*Performance Specs and Mods<BR>*Advertisements<P><BR>This is totally a group effort here so anything you guys want to do--lets hear it!<P>I'd prefer to do the car pages(page file sizes get a little big and hard to transport with good photos), but if you can make a PDF or EPS of the page, feel free to make your own!  You can scan your own pics and give me a ZIP or CD or mail me a photo.  You'll get a front and back of the page.  At least the front in color.<P>I'd like ideas on the cover design, content and whatever!<P>This will be available for order on my website...most likely, I will sell the binder and each section individually so if you don't car for a particular part you don't have to get it.  Price?  Not much.  It won't cost anything to submit your car.  <P>I'm sure we'll agree on that Cliff, and FieroPhil should get a copy at no charge--they do quite a bit for the Fiero community.<BR>Any other nominees?<P>I will post specs here later and have a submission form available on my website.<P>Oh...I'm working on the Fiero playing cards that Urchin suggested.  Probably use pics I get from this.<P>Whaddya think guys?<P>Joe<P>||||reg||4
