Z||000007||AusFiero||08-08-2001||07:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B><BR>I also have a complex (50+ hours) Adobe Illustrator 8 drawing of my Fiero that I worked on last year- It may not look like much to most people, but anyone who has used Illustrator will appreciate it!<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierodraw.jpg">  <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Oh I can appreciate it MinnGreenGT, being a formaly trained graphic artist among my other skills I have picked up over the years. I have Illustrator but for some reason still prefer to use Corel Draw, oh and my alltime favourite of course is Adobe Photoshop, well unless there is a specific need for vector graphics anyway. I often just rough out designs in Corel then take them into Photoshop for their "Paintjobs".<BR>    I have about 100 hours of design in my stage 2 body kit alone. It is coming along well in the plug making stage with so many drawings to work off.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000008||Joe Torma||08-08-2001||08:30 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fiero_24:<BR><B>Didn't Haze already start a book on Fieros?  <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Ah, that's who it was....In the other thread I mentioned that someone wanted to make a book on Fiero History(I just searched through the forum and yes it was Haze) and didn't know who it was.  I had offered my help to him.  He basically wanted to have pictures and write mainly about stock Fieros.  I haven't heard aything more about it.  So Haze, if you haven't started...get going!!!  If you have, well, lets collaberate...<BR>||||reg||2
Z||000009||Joe Torma||08-08-2001||08:36 PM||||MinnGreen...Love the drawing!  Defenitely looks like it took a while!  I guess we should have a Fiero art section!  <P>I'll be waiting for your layout ideas...maybe you could handle the whole GT class.<P>I am flexible on the layout specs.  I won't be outsourcing the job for 4color.  It will be printed with my 2 Fiery Laser printers...Pantone calibrated, so use Pantone (Convert to)Process Colors for accurate colors.  The machines do well with RGB images, so don't worry about CMYK conversion.  I'm sure most of us know about image resolution....more is better, but anything over 225dpi is decent.  So a 640x400 image will look good at about 3"x2"  I would like the main picture to be scanned in and sized at like 250-300dpi.<P>Doing digitally this way makes it easy...and the quality is outstanding.  You will lose about 1/4" at the edges, so no page bleeds.  Page size 8.5x11. <P>If you wish to design your own page, and if this all sounds like greek, let me know.  Otherwise get going!<P>Price?  What's reasonable?  Guessing $15-20 for the inital publication?  Less for updates.<P>Joe<p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 08-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||Fierokid87||08-09-2001||12:01 PM||||Oh so this will basically be like those books that you get some of the pages for in the mail and your supossed to buy the book and order the rest of the pages as they come out?  Im all for it!<P>Scott<P><P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="BLOODY"> Fierokid's  Web site<BR>http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero<P>AIM: Fierokid87<BR>ICQ: Fierokid</FONT><P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sfiero.JPG"> ||||reg||1
